WEBVTT

00:01:29.038 --> 00:01:31.288
And we know
that teeth tell us many things.

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:32.954
For your dentist, for example.

00:01:32.996 --> 00:01:34.829
He or she can see if you floss

00:01:34.871 --> 00:01:38.621
or if, like me, you really like candy,
and you might end up with some cavities.

00:01:38.621 --> 00:01:41.538
And if my dentist is here tonight,
yes, I will see you Monday.

00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:42.788
And I've been very good.

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:45.663
But your teeth also tell you
something about migration.

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:48.996
If you take your tongue
and run it along your incisors,

00:01:49.038 --> 00:01:50.288
these front teeth,

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:54.829
the back of those will be flat
if you have European or African ancestry,

00:01:54.871 --> 00:01:57.538
if you feel a sort of scoop
or shovel shape,

00:01:57.579 --> 00:02:00.996
your ancestors may have been
Native American or migrated from Asia.